TITLE:: REScorePlayer
summary:: Plays an REScore back on its song
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REScore, Classes/REScoreRecorder

DESCRIPTION::
Every event at its recorded beat on the song's clock, from one Routine that waits between events; nothing it does is recorded (link::Classes/RETap#*silently::) and, with the server running, each event's messages go in a code::server.latency:: bundle. How each kind replays, and the fallback to an event's recorded effects, is in the reCording guide ("Replay"). A code::\rawMidi:: event is dispatched through link::Classes/MIDIIn:: as the device would send it, from the device of the recorded name when present.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: score
argument:: song

METHOD:: applyState
argument:: song
argument:: state
A snapshot's state (the event's code::state:: field).
argument:: beats
Numeric sources ramp to their target over this many beats (0: at once).

METHOD:: alignedStart
argument:: score
argument:: clock
argument:: quant
returns:: The next beat on the grid (quant's, else the score's code::quant::, else 1) that is, modulo the grid, where the score's code::beat0:: was.

METHOD:: ramp
argument:: fromValue
argument:: toValue
argument:: beats
argument:: curve
returns:: A Pseg to the target, then the target held.

METHOD:: rampControl
argument:: set
code::{ |value| }::.
argument:: from
argument:: to
argument:: beats
argument:: spec
A take's spec dictionary (min, max, warp), nil for linear.
argument:: clock
argument:: stepsPerBeat
returns:: The Routine stepping the setter to the target along the spec's warp.

METHOD:: controlSpecFor
argument:: spec
returns:: A link::Classes/ControlSpec:: from a take's spec dictionary.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: play
argument:: quant
The grid on the song's clock; the start is on the take's own phase of it (link::#*alignedStart::). nil: the grid the take was recorded on, else the next beat.
argument:: from
argument:: to
Score beats (to nil: the end).
argument:: loop
Play [from, to] again and again (to nil: the score's duration).
argument:: atBeat
An absolute clock beat instead of quant.

METHOD:: stop
METHOD:: isPlaying
METHOD:: position
The score beat the playhead is at, nil when stopped.
METHOD:: passes
Loop passes done.

METHOD:: fire
argument:: ev
Replays one event now. A code line's actions are watched (link::Classes/RETap#*observe::): when the line raises, its recorded effects play from the first one it did not reach (code::fallback:: on the event: code::false:: none, code::true:: all).
returns:: True when it was fired.

METHOD:: mute
METHOD:: unmute
argument:: voices
nil unmutes all.
METHOD:: solo
argument:: voices
nil clears the solo.
METHOD:: defer
argument:: voices
Their sources are not fired: their effects play, and the program events (level 2) under them when the take holds its companion. An event can say so itself with code::defer: true::.
METHOD:: undefer
argument:: voices
nil undefers all.
METHOD:: playOrphans
Program events with no cause play too (false by default: the program does them).
METHOD:: deferredCount
Sources deferred so far.

METHOD:: onEvent
code::{ |player, event| }:: after each fired event.
METHOD:: onLoop
code::{ |player, pass| }:: at each new pass.
METHOD:: onDone
code::{ |player| }:: at the end (not for loops).

METHOD:: alignPhase
Start on the take's phase of the grid (true by default): what the take quantized lands as it did. false: the plain grid.

METHOD:: interpolate
Between two points of an input control (MIDI, OSC, raw MIDI, keyboard), fire interpolated values along the control's spec (false by default: the points, as played); actions on objects are never ramped.
METHOD:: stepsPerBeat
The rate of the ramps (16).
METHOD:: interpolated
Interpolated values fired so far.

METHOD:: followTempo
Apply the recorded tempo events to the clock (false by default).
METHOD:: useLatency
Bundle each event's messages at the server's latency (true).
METHOD:: fired
METHOD:: skipped

EXAMPLES::

code::
~p = REScorePlayer(REScore.read(~piece_dir +/+ "Scores/261001_143012_demo w1.json"), ~song);
~p.play([4, 0]);
~p.play(from: 8, to: 16, loop: true);
~p.stop;
::
